iOS BLOCKER (pre-existing sibling compile errors — NOT in scope, NOT DataTable)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The whole `TeslaSync` app target compiles ~3,000 sources into one module. Two
sibling sources fail to compile; because Swift compiles a module atomically, the
whole target (and therefore the hosted test bundle) fails. Exact errors:

  1) TeslaSync/feature-views/RecentDrivesSection.Previews.swift:24:20: error:
     the compiler is unable to type-check this expression in reasonable time;
     try breaking up the expression into distinct sub-expressions

  2) TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/AISignalExplorerNlFilter.swift:142:22: error:
     escaping closure captures non-escaping parameter 'content'
     (sibling bug: `glass(@ViewBuilder _ content: () -> some View)` passes the
      non-escaping `content` into `TSGlassPanel { content() }`, whose builder is
      @escaping. Fix belongs in AISignalExplorerNlFilter.swift — out of scope.)

